\h Psalms
\toc1 Psalms
\mt1 Psalms
\c 23
\s1 The \nd Lord\nd* Is My Shepherd
\d A Psalm of David.
\q1
\v 1 The \nd Lord\nd* is my shepherd; I shall not want.
\q2 
\v 2 He makes me lie down in green pastures.
\q1 He leads me beside still waters.\f + \ft Hebrew beside waters of rest\f*
\q2 
\v 3 He restores my soul.
\q1 He leads me in paths of righteousness\f + \ft Or in right paths\f*
\q2 for his name's sake.
\q1
\v 4 Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,\f + \ft Or the valley of deep darkness\f*
\q2 I will fear no evil,
\q1 for you are with me;
\q2 your rod and your staff,
\q2 they comfort me.
\q1
\v 5 You prepare a table before me
\q2 in the presence of my enemies;
\q1 you anoint my head with oil;
\q2 my cup overflows.
\q1
\v 6 Surely\f + \ft Or Only\f* goodness and mercy\f + \ft Or steadfast love\f* shall follow me
\q2 all the days of my life,
\q1 and I shall dwell\f + \ft Or shall return to dwell\f* in the house of the \nd Lord\nd*
\q2 forever.\f + \ft Hebrew for length of days\f*
